    "title": "<p>Diagnostic criteria for T-prolymphocytic leukaemia (T-PLL) according to consensus guidelines {31292114}</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "de Jong D\r\nIs basically the table from the article, so have updated the source.",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 18cm; background: #daeef3; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"680\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 18cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"680\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Essential (major) diagnostic criteria</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 18cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"680\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Peripheral blood lymphocytosis &gt;&nbsp;5&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;10<sup>9</sup>/L or bone marrow infiltrate with T-PLL immunophenotype</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Evidence of T-cell monoclonality</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Demonstration of <em>TCL1A</em> (14q32) or <em>MTCP1</em> (Xq28) rearrangement (desirable identification of juxtaposed TR locus, most frequently TRD) or TCL1A protein expression<sup>a</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 18cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"680\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Minor diagnostic criteria (at least one required)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 18cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"680\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Abnormalities involving chromosome&nbsp;11 (11q22.3, <em>ATM</em>)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Abnormalities in chromosome&nbsp;8: idic(8)(p11), t(8;8), trisomy 8q</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Abnormalities in chromosome&nbsp;5, 12, 13, or 22, or complex karyotype</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Involvement of specific sites (e.g. splenomegaly, effusions)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p><sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\">a</span></sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\">In</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"> 90&ndash;95% of cases, the diagnosis is established by all three major criteria being met. For discussion of (and diagnostic criteria for) TCL1-negative T-PLL, see the text <span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\">{37443196}</span>.</span></p>",
